From 38fdbaa910c6f5d5bd9803b219ccc1da96418d13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sachin <sachinbarange86@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:45:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Unlock Dual Video multi-camera mode (port of upstream 0009)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Upstream 0009 rewrote three self-instanceof capability checks in the stock
dump's obfuscated device-config class. In the dyper dump that class kept its
real name: smali_classes3/device_common.smali (500 methods, .super
Ljava/lang/Object;, 252 "instance-of p0, p0, L...;" capability probes).

Only Ldevice_common;->T3()Z actually gates Dual Video:

  smali_classes5/com/xiaomi/microfilm/dualcam/mode/DualCamModuleEntry  -> support()
  smali_classes5/com/xiaomi/microfilm/dualcam/mode/DualVideoRecordModule
  smali_classes5/com/xiaomi/microfilm/ui/FragmentMicroFilm

T3() resolved through Lv7/b;->e:Ldevice_common; (virtual dispatch on the
per-device instance, which for this phone is Lonyx;). Neither Lonyx; nor its
parent Lredmi_phone2; override T3(), so patching the base is enough.

The check was "instance-of p0, p0, L䚋...;" - a leaf device class in the
Lredmi_phone4; lineage. The onyx chain is
onyx -> redmi_phone2 -> device_common -> Object, so it evaluated false and the
mode stayed hidden. Forced to true.

The other two hunks of upstream 0009 (c3()Z and the @Deprecated W2()Z, both set
to 0x0 there) are NOT ported: they test the same leaf class, so on onyx they
already return false and rewriting them would be a pure no-op. c3()Z has only
two callers, both in smali/X5/f.smali, and neither is on the Dual Video path.

Signed-off-by: Sachin <sachinbarange86@gmail.com>
---
 smali_classes3/device_common.smali | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/smali_classes3/device_common.smali b/smali_classes3/device_common.smali
index d2f7b2fc..61efecf8 100644
--- a/smali_classes3/device_common.smali
+++ b/smali_classes3/device_common.smali
@@ -1725,7 +1725,7 @@
 .method public T3()Z
     .locals 0
 
-    instance-of p0, p0, L䚋䚇䚅䛆䚅䚁䛆䚌䚍䚞䚁䚋䚍䛆䚭䚅䚍䚚䚉䚄䚌䚷䚘䚚䚇䚷䚚;
+    const/4 p0, 0x1
 
     return p0
 .end method
